# Known-broken links caused by upstream @takazudo/zudo-doc limitations, not by
# this project's content. Every entry must name the upstream issue and be
# removable once that issue ships a fix.
#
# Entry forms:
#   file:line:href   pins one occurrence (precise, but breaks if lines shift)
#   href=<href>      allows that href wherever it appears
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CURRENTLY EMPTY — the link check passes with no exceptions.
#
# It previously held 8 `href=` entries for zudolab/zudo-doc#3196 (the version
# switcher offers a snapshot link for a page that exists only in newer docs
# instead of greying it out). All of them pointed into /v/1.0/, and the 1.0
# snapshot has been removed, so those links are no longer emitted at all.
#
# #3196 is NOT fixed upstream — it is only dormant, because the single
# remaining snapshot (2.0) has every page Latest has. It will resurface the
# moment a doc page is added to Latest without re-snapshotting, or another
# snapshot is added. When it does, prefer the `href=` form: pinning one entry
# per occurrence rots on the next content edit that shifts a line number.
#
# Keep this file even while empty — check-links.js is invoked with
# --allowlist=.check-links-allowlist in package.json, and the header above is
# the only place the two entry forms are documented.
